  "caption": "Quinn's first night as a line cook: twelve hours on hard floors, a very low fridge, and feet on fire by hour ten.\n\nLong standing, repeated bending, lifting pots and stock at pace, heat and late finishes can all add up across a shift. Aches are common in kitchens, but they don't have to be part of the uniform.\n\nWhat often helps: supportive, non-slip shoes replaced when worn, anti-fatigue mats at fixed stations, sharp knives to ease grip force, mini moves like calf raises and shoulder rolls between orders, plus water and proper breaks.\n\nHeel, arch or wrist pain that won't settle is worth getting checked. Deep cuts or burns to the hand need prompt medical care.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
